
  [34mfunction[39m [33mlogin[39m(username, password, userId) {
    console.[33mlog[39m([31m"Logging in:"[39m, username, [31m"userId:"[39m, userId);
    [32m// Stub: would POST { username, password, userId } to API_ENDPOINT[39m
    [34mreturn[39m { [36msuccess[39m: [34mtrue[39m, [36muser[39m: username, userId };
  }
  - The submit handler calls [38;5;153mlogin(username, password, getUserId())[39m. [38;5;153mlogin[39m itself never reads storage. It just receives
    the ID, which keeps it pure, and future forms follow the same pattern of calling [38;5;153mgetUserId()[39m and passing the result.
  - [38;5;153muserId[39m is included in the stubbed payload comment and in the return value, so whatever uses the result can see who
    logged in.
  - [38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m doesn't change, because the userId isn't user input.

  [1m[38;5;153mindex.html[39m:[0m [38;5;153m<script src="app.js">[39m becomes [38;5;153m<script type="module" src="app.js">[39m. Modules are deferred automatically, so
  the [38;5;153mgetElementById[39m wiring still runs after the DOM loads.

  [1mData flow:[0m submit → [38;5;153mgetUserId()[39m (from localStorage, or newly generated and saved) → [38;5;153mlogin(username, password, userId)[39m
  → logged and returned.

  [1mServing:[0m a README note says to run [38;5;153mnpx serve .[39m (or any static server) and open it over HTTP, because modules don't
  load from [38;5;153mfile://[39m.

  [1mSection 3: Testing[0m

  - [1m[38;5;153midentity.test.js[0m uses Node's built-in [38;5;153mnode:test[39m with a fake storage object. It checks that the first call generates
    and saves a UUID, that a later call returns the same value, that an existing stored value is reused, and that a
    storage which throws still returns an ID.
  - Node 26 detects ESM syntax on its own, so [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m doesn't need [38;5;153m"type": "module"[39m. That matters because adding it
    would break the CommonJS [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m. I'll add [38;5;153m"test": "node --test"[39m to the scripts.
  - [38;5;153mlogin[39m stays in [38;5;153mapp.js[39m, which needs the DOM, so I'll check it in a real browser over HTTP: the console should show
    the same userId across a reload.

  Do Sections 2 and 3 look right? Once you approve, I'll write the spec to
  [38;5;153mdocs/hyperpowers/specs/2026-10-03-login-userid-design.md[39m (uncommitted) for you to review before any code is written.

